diff --git a/docs/gguf-nvfp4-prefill.md b/docs/gguf-nvfp4-prefill.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ce569683babb8347ad9b83e2c178d11c7f57b560
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/gguf-nvfp4-prefill.md
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+# Experimental GGUF NVFP4 prefill
+
+`NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_NVFP4=1` admits NVFP4 products of GGUF matrices whose logical
+Use grants `AllowA4`. Set the variable before model loading; unset or `0` keeps
+the normal route. This experiment is qualified separately from the MXFP8
+experiment. The NVFP4 qualification uses `NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_MXFP8=0`.
+
+The stored GGUF blocks remain the model's weights. Wide products decode bounded
+slabs into E2M1 values with an E4M3 scale per 16 values and a power-of-two global
+per operand. Four candidate scales are compared with FP16 error sums. GEMM uses
+FP32 accumulation and BF16 output. Gate/up products round to BF16 before SiLU.
+The fused feed-forward producer encodes that same BF16 intermediate for down,
+preserving the separate producer's rounding boundary. Globals are bounded to
+`2^-60..2^60` to keep the combined FP32 multiplier finite; very small/large values
+can underflow or saturate, as with the other low-precision representations.
+
+The route requires an sm120 device/build, K divisible by 256, and cuBLASLt's
+block-scaled GEMM. It supports IQ1_S, IQ1_M, IQ2_XXS, IQ2_XS, IQ2_S, IQ3_XXS,
+IQ3_S, IQ4_XS, Q2_K, Q4_K and Q6_K. It begins at 129 columns, above every
+supported decode/verification batch. BF16 Store and Accumulate destinations
+require 16-byte aligned columns; other destinations and unsupported products
+keep their previous arithmetic. Load-time preparation is currently connected
+to Qwen3.5-family Parameters, including its MTP/draft and rank operands.
+
+Parameters own the immutable weight maxima and scale-choice cache. Each cache
+records two bits per 16 weights, rounded to 128 bytes per operand, in pinned host
+memory; identical operands at one global share a table. Calls own their transient
+activation and image slabs through the Program workspace. No permanent FP4 copy
+of model weights is created. Preparation adds startup work and host memory.
+Precision mode is included in prefill signatures and session snapshot bindings.
+
+KVMem's statistics-copy adapter also coalesces contiguous layers into one 2D
+transfer per rank. Key and Query runs remain separate; partial accepted Query
+prefixes keep their original per-layer gaps. This changes transfer scheduling,
+without changing any statistics bytes, Query/Pressure decisions or precision.
+The host `ninfer_memory_statistics_layout` test checks independent whole-buffer
+values and canaries for unequal head shards, layer partitions, Mean-Q and
+partial/full Query prefixes, with both separate and coalesced copies.
+
+An existing GGUF artifact often grants only `AllowA8`. A permission-only copy can
+be created through the artifact writer, without changing physical tensor bytes:
+
+```powershell
+python -m tools.artifact.gguf_a4 SOURCE.ninfer A4.ninfer --scope all-projections --report a4.json
+$env:NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_NVFP4 = '1'
+$env:NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_MXFP8 = '0'
+.\ninfer-serve.exe A4.ninfer --prefill-chunk 1024
+```
+
+`--scope mlp-gate-up` grants A4 only to text-layer MLP gate/up Uses; attention,
+down projections, output heads and sensitive Uses retain their permissions. The
+`mlp-gate-up-middle-half` scope further restricts this to the middle half of text
+layers (16 through 47 in the measured 64-layer model). The
+tool promotes only existing GGUF `AllowA8` Uses, writes a new artifact identity,
+and verifies each physical object's hash after copying. It requires space for a
+second artifact. Existing `A16Only` Uses and other physical formats are preserved.
+
+NVFP4 adds quantization error. Passing a bounded corpus and recall suite is a
+qualification of that model/profile/workload, rather than a universal quality
+guarantee. Keep the experiment off until the intended profile passes its speed
+and quality criteria. Benchmark with the same GPU UUID and settings; use
+`NINFER_PREFILL_ALIGN=0` when measuring exact requested chunk widths.
+
+The native `ninfer_linear_gguf_nvfp4_test` qualifies codecs, independently decoded
+packed weights, FP64 products, residuals, SwiGLU, fused down production, mapped
+host scale caches, workspace bounds, canaries, graph replay and fallback widths.
+Run it on an idle sm120 GPU with the NVFP4 variable set to `1`. Run its
+`--boundary-only` form with the variable both `0` and `1` and compare the printed
+checksum to check protected q8 calls.
